IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: the Fourteenth, Fifteenth and Sixteenth Schedules (Part 11A: registers of controllers).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Part sgm. Text: the SSO informal consolidation as the file renders it (a rendering, not the official text).
-- The Seventh to Eleventh Schedules are shown repealed and have coverage rows only; the Twelfth and Thirteenth are wave 1's (sgc1, sgc2).
--
-- These Schedules are definitions for Part 11A (encoded elsewhere): which companies and foreign companies Part 11A does not apply to, what "significant control"
-- and "significant interest" mean, and how interests and rights are counted. A borrowed fact (listed on an exchange, wholly owned by the Government, exempted under another Act)
-- is a plain input. READING A RESULT: JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say".

§ `Fourteenth Schedule paragraph 2: a Singapore financial institution`

-- "2. For the purposes of paragraph 1, a Singapore financial institution is -- (a) any financial institution that is licensed, approved, registered or regulated by the Monetary Authority of Singapore
-- but does not include -- (i) [Deleted] (ii) a person (other than a person mentioned in sub-paragraphs (b) and (c)) who is exempted from licensing, approval or regulation by the Monetary Authority ...;
-- (b) any person exempted under section 20(1)(g) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 ...; or (c) any person exempted under section 99(1)(h) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 ..."
-- The definition names its own heads and hands the term to them (delegated-definitions ruling (a)): when no head holds, JUST FALSE.
-- The exclusion in (a)(ii) does not reach a person mentioned in (b) or (c), who is a Singapore financial institution by those paragraphs in any case.
-- src:29352 | 2. For the purposes of paragraph 1, a Singapore financial institution is —
-- src:29354 | (a) any financial institution that is licensed, approved, registered or
-- src:29355 | regulated by the Monetary Authority of Singapore but does not
-- src:29356 | include —
-- src:29360 | (ii) a person (other than a person mentioned in sub‑paragraphs (b)
-- src:29361 | and (c)) who is exempted from licensing, approval or
-- src:29362 | regulation by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under
-- src:29363 | any Act administered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore,
-- src:29364 | including a private trust company exempted from licensing
-- src:29365 | under section 15 of the Trust Companies Act 2005 read with
-- src:29366 | regulation 4 of the Trust Companies (Exemption) Regulations;
-- src:29370 | (b) any person exempted under section 20(1)(g) of the Financial Advisers
-- src:29371 | Act 2001 read with regulation 27(1)(d) of the Financial Advisers
-- src:29372 | Regulations; or
-- src:29374 | (c) any person exempted under section 99(1)(h) of the Securities and
-- src:29375 | Futures Act 2001 read with paragraph 7(1)(b) of the Second Schedule
-- src:29376 | to the Securities and Futures (Licensing and Conduct of Business)
-- src:29377 | Regulations.
@ref sch 14 para 2 (src:29352-29377)
GIVEN `the person is a financial institution licensed, approved, registered or regulated by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted from licensing, approval or regulation by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under an Act administered by it (including a private trust company exempted under section 15 of the Trust Companies Act 2005 read with regulation 4 of the Trust Companies (Exemption) Regulations)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted under section 20(1)(g) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 read with regulation 27(1)(d) of the Financial Advisers Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted under section 99(1)(h) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 read with paragraph 7(1)(b) of the Second Schedule to the Securities and Futures (Licensing and Conduct of Business) Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 14 para 2 the person is a Singapore financial institution` MEANS
    IF     (`the person is a financial institution licensed, approved, registered or regulated by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` AND (NOT `the person is exempted from licensing, approval or regulation by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under an Act administered by it (including a private trust company exempted under section 15 of the Trust Companies Act 2005 read with regulation 4 of the Trust Companies (Exemption) Regulations)`))
        OR `the person is exempted under section 20(1)(g) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 read with regulation 27(1)(d) of the Financial Advisers Regulations`
        OR `the person is exempted under section 99(1)(h) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 read with paragraph 7(1)(b) of the Second Schedule to the Securities and Futures (Licensing and Conduct of Business) Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; delegated-definitions ruling (a)): "a Singapore financial institution is -- (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." (a definition that names its heads; none holds)

-- (a)(ii) excludes a person exempted from licensing "other than a person mentioned in sub-paragraphs (b) and (c)": the person exempted under (b) or (c) is in by those paragraphs.
-- src:29352 | 2. For the purposes of paragraph 1, a Singapore financial institution is —
-- src:29354 | (a) any financial institution that is licensed, approved, registered or
-- src:29355 | regulated by the Monetary Authority of Singapore but does not
-- src:29356 | include —
-- src:29360 | (ii) a person (other than a person mentioned in sub‑paragraphs (b)
-- src:29361 | and (c)) who is exempted from licensing, approval or
-- src:29362 | regulation by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under
-- src:29363 | any Act administered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore,
-- src:29364 | including a private trust company exempted from licensing
-- src:29365 | under section 15 of the Trust Companies Act 2005 read with
-- src:29366 | regulation 4 of the Trust Companies (Exemption) Regulations;
@ref sch 14 para 2(a) (src:29352-29366)
GIVEN `the person is a financial institution licensed, approved, registered or regulated by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted from licensing, approval or regulation by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under an Act administered by it (including a private trust company exempted under section 15 of the Trust Companies Act 2005 read with regulation 4 of the Trust Companies (Exemption) Regulations)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 14 para 2(a) the financial institution is within paragraph (a)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a financial institution licensed, approved, registered or regulated by the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    THEN (IF `the person is exempted from licensing, approval or regulation by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under an Act administered by it (including a private trust company exempted under section 15 of the Trust Companies Act 2005 read with regulation 4 of the Trust Companies (Exemption) Regulations)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any financial institution that is licensed, approved, registered or regulated by the Monetary Authority of Singapore but does not include ... (ii) a person ... who is exempted from licensing, approval or regulation" (the exclusion is met; a person also mentioned in paragraph (b) or (c) is in by that paragraph)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) any financial institution that is licensed, approved, registered or regulated by the Monetary Authority of Singapore" (a limb of a definition that names its heads; the person is not one)

§ `Fourteenth Schedule paragraph 1: companies to which Part 11A does not apply`

-- (f): shares listed on a securities exchange outside Singapore, subject to (i) regulatory disclosure requirements and (ii) requirements for adequate transparency of beneficial owners, imposed through stock exchange rules, law or other enforceable means.
-- The render prints the closing words with the label "(f)" a second time; they are the closing words of (f) (finding 4 in NOTES.md).
-- src:29334 | (f) a company which shares are listed on a securities exchange in a
-- src:29335 | country or territory outside Singapore and which is subject to —
-- src:29337 | (i) regulatory disclosure requirements; and
-- src:29339 | (ii) requirements relating to adequate transparency in respect of its
-- src:29340 | beneficial owners,
-- src:29342 | (f) imposed through stock exchange rules, law or other enforceable
-- src:29343 | means.
@ref sch 14 para 1(f) (src:29334-29343)
GIVEN `the company's shares are listed on a securities exchange in a country or territory outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is subject to regulatory disclosure requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is subject to requirements relating to adequate transparency in respect of its beneficial owners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those requirements are imposed through stock exchange rules, law or other enforceable means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 14 para 1(f) the company is within paragraph 1(f)` MEANS
        `the company's shares are listed on a securities exchange in a country or territory outside Singapore`
    AND `the company is subject to regulatory disclosure requirements`
    AND `the company is subject to requirements relating to adequate transparency in respect of its beneficial owners`
    AND `those requirements are imposed through stock exchange rules, law or other enforceable means`

-- src:29318 | 1. Subject to section 386AA(1A), Part 11A does not apply to any of the
-- src:29319 | following companies:
-- src:29321 | (a) a public company which shares are listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:29322 | exchange in Singapore;
-- src:29324 | (b) a company that is a Singapore financial institution;
-- src:29326 | (c) a company that is wholly‑owned by the Government;
-- src:29328 | (d) a company that is wholly‑owned by a statutory body established by or
-- src:29329 | under a public Act for a public purpose;
-- src:29331 | (e) a company that is a wholly‑owned subsidiary of a company mentioned
-- src:29332 | in sub‑paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d);
-- src:29334 | (f) a company which shares are listed on a securities exchange in a
-- src:29335 | country or territory outside Singapore and which is subject to —
-- src:29337 | (i) regulatory disclosure requirements; and
-- src:29339 | (ii) requirements relating to adequate transparency in respect of its
-- src:29340 | beneficial owners,
-- src:29342 | (f) imposed through stock exchange rules, law or other enforceable
-- src:29343 | means.
@ref sch 14 para 1 (src:29318-29343)
GIVEN `section 386AA(1A) makes Part 11A apply to the company despite this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a Singapore financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is wholly owned by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is wholly owned by a statutory body established by or under a public Act for a public purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a wholly owned subsidiary of a company mentioned in sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is within paragraph 1(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 14 para 1 Part 11A does not apply to the company` MEANS
    IF `section 386AA(1A) makes Part 11A apply to the company despite this paragraph`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-U1): "Subject to section 386AA(1A), Part 11A does not apply to any of the following companies" ("Subject to" met: section 386AA(1A) is not among the sources and is taken as a fact)
    ELSE (IF     `the company is a public company whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange in Singapore`
              OR `the company is a Singapore financial institution`
              OR `the company is wholly owned by the Government`
              OR `the company is wholly owned by a statutory body established by or under a public Act for a public purpose`
              OR `the company is a wholly owned subsidiary of a company mentioned in sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)`
              OR `the company is within paragraph 1(f)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Part 11A does not apply to any of the following companies" -- a list not closed with "only"; for any other company the text here says nothing (section 386AA says to whom Part 11A applies)

§ `Fifteenth Schedule: foreign companies to which Part 11A does not apply`

-- (c): the same test as Fourteenth Schedule paragraph 1(f), for a foreign company.
