-- 4(6)(b): "'arrangement' includes (i) any scheme, agreement or understanding, whether or not it is legally enforceable; and (ii) any convention, custom or practice of any kind, but something does not count
-- as an arrangement unless there is at least some degree of stability about it". The render prints the closing words with the label "(b)" a second time (finding 4 in NOTES.md).
-- src:29509 | (6) In this paragraph —
-- src:29521 | (b) “arrangement” includes —
-- src:29523 | (i) any scheme, agreement or understanding, whether or not it is
-- src:29524 | legally enforceable; and
-- src:29526 | (ii) any convention, custom or practice of any kind,
-- src:29528 | (b) but something does not count as an arrangement unless there is at least
-- src:29529 | some degree of stability about it (whether by its nature or terms, the
-- src:29530 | time it has been in existence or otherwise).
@ref sch 16 para 4(6)(b) (src:29509-29530)
GIVEN `the thing is a scheme, agreement or understanding, whether or not it is legally enforceable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a convention, custom or practice of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is at least some degree of stability about it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 16 para 4(6)(b) the thing counts as an arrangement` MEANS
    IF NOT `there is at least some degree of stability about it`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "something does not count as an arrangement unless there is at least some degree of stability about it" ("unless" not met)
    ELSE (IF `the thing is a scheme, agreement or understanding, whether or not it is legally enforceable` OR `the thing is a convention, custom or practice of any kind`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "'arrangement' includes (i) any scheme, agreement or understanding ...; and (ii) any convention, custom or practice of any kind" -- an "includes" list; the text says nothing of any other thing
